{
  "summary": "This experiment tested whether adding the image modality (ResNet50, avgpool) via simple concat fusion to the strongest RNA-only multiprofile backbone (scvi_n200, avgpool) would push beyond the ~65% RNA-only ceiling. The validation accuracy of ~63.2% (F1 ~60.7%) is slightly below the RNA-only multiprofile avgpool baseline (~65.0%), an initial observation suggesting that the residual image signal does not provide complementary predictive information under this configuration and may introduce mild interference, though the ~1.8-point gap is small and the specific contributor (image content, ResNet50 encoder quality, or the concat mechanism) cannot be isolated from this single experiment. It remains uncertain whether alternative fusion strategies (e.g., weighted or attention-based), stronger image encoders, or different image-branch aggregation could recover or exceed the RNA-only performance, or whether the image modality is fundamentally non-complementary for this task."
}

